  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Environmental and Economic Feasibility Study and Detailed Design of One-Stop-Border-Post (OSBP) and Bypass Road at Tog Wajaale, Somaliland</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the development cooperation is two-fold: 
1)	To carry out an &#x201c;Inclusive, Sustainable, and Climate-focused Feasibility Study and Infrastructure Needs Assessment&#x201d; for developing border related infrastructure to serve as a juxtaposed One-Stop-Border Post (OSBP) at the border town of Tog Wajaale (Somaliland and Ethiopia). The feasibility will take a regional approach and will include both hard infrastructure and soft infrastructure. In addition to infrastructure needs assessment, the consultancy firm will be help in identifying and designing a series of complementary interventions to upgrade the border operations and best implementation and financing options. All these will be undertaken under a sustainability lens that ensures mitigation of environmental and social risks whilst enhancing beneficial opportunities for green approaches that ensure facilities become more climate change, environment and socially sustainable. 

2)	To carry out the &#x201c;Detailed Architectural and Engineering Designs,&#x201d; including green concepts for the approved infrastructure arising from the feasibility study and needs assessment subject to satisfactory completion of the first phase.</narrative>
  </description>
